    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0054" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857.48/3–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-28T18:00:00-04:00">March 28, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2403. From Department and FEA for EWD. ReEmbs 3045, March 23,<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d34-f1"/> paragraph C–7. American authorities are agreeable to
                    immediate shipment of 6700 tons seed grain from Sweden to Norway under
                    supervision JSC,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d34-f2"/> Stockholm. It is understood
                    that MEW agrees. Inform Stockholm of joint decision. Department endeavoring
                    expedite consideration other pending Norwegian relief proposals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
